{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/162767-sell-me-on-promethean","id":162767,"title":"Sell me on Promethean","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-08T15:28:49-07:00","id":162767,"title":"Sell me on Promethean","content":"I've got the book, and I've tried and failed to get into this line. So, three questions: 1. What's great about Promethean? 2. What kind of stories does it lend itself to? 3. Using that vague statement of &quot;Demons are spies, Makes are detectives...&quot;, what are Prometheans, in a broad sense? (I'm really keen to see how people see the other races - vampires, werewolves, changeling, sin - eaters and mummies - but it is a tangential thing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3192-baileyborough","name":"baileyborough","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T16:04:13-07:00","id":162863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baileyborough</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/162767-sell-me-on-promethean#post162767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got the book, and I've tried and failed to get into this line. So, three questions: 1. What's great about Promethean? 2. What kind of stories does it lend itself to? 3. Using that vague statement of &quot;Demons are spies, Makes are detectives...&quot;, what are Prometheans, in a broad sense? (I'm really keen to see how people see the other races - vampires, werewolves, changeling, sin - eaters and mummies - but it is a tangential thing).</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Promethean is game about monsters trying to learn what it's like to be human. It's a being that has born out not out of love or lust but either unbridled obsession of a person or by a monster who him/herself is coming at the end of the road and fumbling through a world that actively hates them on a fundamental level.<br /> <br /> 2. Personal ones mostly. Sure some Promethean stories can lead to epic tier 3 conflict but at the end of the game, you're going to have to explained what your character learned about humanity from that conflict to continue down his path.<br /> <br /> 3. Prometheans are hated homeless pilgrims attempting to gain salvation via their works. They can also throw people/things into the next continent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T17:34:46-07:00","id":162994,"title":"","content":"1. Promethean is a philosophical game where you get to put every single thing we (humans) do casually everyday into perspective: Why prostitution? Why gambling? Why drugs &amp; alcohol? Why taking a shower everyday? If someone has food to feed 10 000 humans, why does he let a homeless guy die by his store?<br /> <br /> 2. As shock said: personal ones. You can tell a story with a huge plot that spans the continent but you will not get what Promethean is as long as you don't play the scene where he finally buys that doll he's been looking for.<br /> <br /> 3. Prometheans are kids in the body of an adult: they shuffle around not truly understanding what is going on, but are expected to know and act correctly: because they are adults.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/162767-sell-me-on-promethean?p=162863#post162863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can also throw people/things into the next continent.</div> </div> </div> </div>This cannot be overstated. Many of their powers are terrifying in nature, because they are not supposed to be heroes since nature itself wants them hated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T20:16:44-07:00","id":163082,"title":"","content":"It's funny that every so often someone wants to be sold on promethean. Your specific questions have already been addressed, but I would like to elaborate to some degree.<br /> <br /> The biggest difference that sold me is how the characters are actually on a philosophical journey to becoming human. Not in some vague way either, but specifically with milestones on a pilgrimage. Also, how there are multiple ways of getting there depending on the character's refinement and just pure character outlook. Instead of being motivated by money, power, status, just staying alive, etc. the characters are developed slowly with that clear goal in mind.<br /> <br /> Also, I like how the character's disquiet and wasteland forces them to keep moving. It's kinda cool how much characterization can stem from that.<br /> <br /> Personally, I love the potential a promethean chronicle has. It is a much different game than Vampire or Mage or any other game I have played.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}